5.  WHERE
Filters individual rows before grouping.
Cannot use aggregate functions directly.

Example: Show orders with amount greater than 300

```
SELECT * FROM Orders
WHERE amount > 300;
```

  HAVING 
Filters groups after GROUP BY.
Used with aggregate functions such as COUNT(), SUM(), AVG().

Example: Show users whose total spending is greater than 800

```
SELECT user_id, SUM(amount) AS total_spend
FROM Orders
GROUP BY user_id
HAVING SUM(amount) > 800;
```





